id: pm-vitestmanual
title: Patch Vitest manual-mock registration code injection
description: "Public mocker/interceptor WebSocket manual registration can interpolate an attacker-controlled URL or export name into JavaScript, including asynchronous rebinding. Requires a reachable public handler; tracked Node test configs do not register it, so application exploitability is not established. Upstream: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qxg6-89mg-rqv8. The locked development dependency is affected; version4.1.12 is patched."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: dependencies,security,vitest
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:12:27.675Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T22:02:44.491Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T22:02:43.065Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T22:02:43.065Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "Inspect the upstream shared boundary and alternate representations; Preserve legitimate test and benchmark behavior; Verify exact lock, fresh advisories and native Windows CI before merge"
parent: pm-vitest4112
risk: medium
confidence: 95
severity: medium
resolution: "Upgrade the compatible Vitest4/coverage pair to4.1.12, add real public-handler before/after regressions and select them in the required Windows native cohort. Strengthen the existing workflow contract and recurrence family without changing cooldown, Vite/CodSpeed compatibility, coverage thresholds or CI budgets."
expected_result: "The affected locked dependency is removed, legitimate behavior is preserved, and the same advisory boundary tests run under both Ubuntu coverage and required Windows path semantics before merge."
actual_result: "Original handler probes fail on4.1.11 and pass on4.1.12; the native-selection contract fails before the workflow step and passes afterward. Linked local checks pass31/31, build/typecheck/lint pass, and fresh full-lock feeds are rechecked. The required native Windows step is now selected and must pass on the final head before merge; no earlier Windows advisory execution is claimed."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:12:27.675Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status corpus3042/3042 including closed items has no occurrence of either advisory or predecessor GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9. Live request-specific searches and open/in_progress inventories found no exact advisory owner; semantic-only search results are not duplicate evidence. Reuse the security epic; keep the broader Vitest5 migration separately open."
  "2026-10-21T21:16:55.092Z","harness:codex","Boundary and compatibility evidence: both public plugin regressions fail against4.1.11 and pass against4.1.12. The generated-source test executes only a harmless synthetic sentinel in a disposable Node child and also verifies exact URL preservation, quotes/backslashes/newlines in export names and asynchronous binding updates. The redirect test exercises the real registration handler and Vite allowlist without reading any files, rejects slash/backslash and nested escapes, and preserves an allowed redirect. This tests the normalization-to-allowlist boundary portably; native Windows CI remains required before merge. No tracked application config registers these public handlers, so no CLI/SDK exploit is claimed."
  "2026-10-21T21:16:56.183Z","harness:codex","Fresh patched evidence at21:13UTC: both feeds complete over all568 locked versions with zero positives; the previous hosted569-version receipt remains the positive before-control. Frozen installation, build and all typecheck targets pass. Existing retry/reporter/CodSpeed runtime cohort passes7/7, new handler regressions pass2/2, and the dedicated benchmark invocation succeeds. Paired4.1.12 packages satisfy pnpm default one-day age without exclusions; Vitest5 and CodSpeed6 migration remains separate."
  "2026-10-21T21:19:10.680Z","harness:codex",Independent candidate review found no concrete surviving bypass or regression. It traced all three shared serialization sites and redirect normalization before allowlist admission and the unchanged checked-path read. Additional read-only controls covered nine redirect representations and five export-name classes. Linux boundary execution passed; native Windows acceptance and whole-project coverage are required hosted gates before merging this reviewed delivery.
  "2026-10-21T21:59:35.024Z","harness:codex","Pre-merge verification correction: final required Windows jobs pass, but their focused native cohort does not select the new installed-mocker boundary file; Ubuntu coverage alone does not satisfy the recorded native Windows acceptance criterion. Reopen this canonical lineage before editing the existing Windows cohort and its workflow contract. Preserve earlier before/after controls and closure history; no duplicate issue or weakened check is needed."
  "2026-10-21T22:02:39.180Z","harness:codex","Windows selection repair: the existing partition contract fails before the native advisory step is added (missing step), then passes with the suite selected only in the native cohort. The complete local workflow+handler cohort passes24/24, and linked dependency/retry/reporter plus workflow commands pass31/31. Build/typecheck/lint/workflow permissions pass. Preserve all three Windows partitions, the12-minute cohort budget and strict aggregate outcomes. Prior head f304eb2 passed26 required checks and100% coverage, but did not run these advisory probes on Windows; the new reviewed head must prove that native step before merge."
